    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) draws an exceptional matchup against Van Eyk, whose 6.05 xERA provides the highest ceiling for our lineup; the combination of a massive park factor boost and the dynamic platoon advantage makes him a must-start at the MI slot. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21) remains a high-floor play despite the tough matchup against Bassitt, largely because the favorable park factors and his placement in the two-hole elevate his run-scoring potential significantly. We are also leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.37), both of whom capitalize on soft opposing rotations and high-leverage lineup spots to anchor our counting stats.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Wade Meckler**, whose 49.31 score fell just short of the efficiency threshold needed to supplant our existing starters. While **Wade Meckler** benefits from an elite SP skill matchup against Springs, he ultimately lost the tie-breaker to **Nasim Nunez** (57.00); though **Nasim Nunez** carries a suboptimal nine-hole assignment, the optimizer favored his elite speed profile and the slow delivery of Valdez, F, which creates a prime window for stolen base accumulation\u2014a priority given our scarcity concerns. Meanwhile, the lineup faces a calculated risk with **Jackson Merrill** (53.11), who draws a difficult assignment against Yamamoto; we are keeping **Jackson Merrill** active due to his moderate stolen base potential, but his output will be capped by the SP\u2019s high skill level. With **Luis Robert Jr.** officially sidelined on the IL, we are closely monitoring lineup confirmations for any late-breaking weather disruptions, but otherwise, our core is positioned to maximize both raw output and the specific category requirements of our Roto pursuit.",
